   208	## 4. Part (2): `N` on a Moh skeleton
   209	
   210	### 4.1 What Moh's tree is, and how the two towers share their structure
   211	
   212	Moh's characteristic data `{M_i, d_i}` is the tree datum of the roots of `f` over
   213	`k[x]((g^{-1/n}))` (`moh.txt:527-573`); from §4 on he studies the **`t`-adic** tree
