   302	### 4.4 THEOREM N-CEILING
   303	
   304	By NU-TWO the root ball `D_s` has **exactly two** children: the major slope class
   305	`D_{s-1}` (`ue` roots of `g`, `ud` of `f`) and the minor class `D*_{s-1}`
   306	(`ve`, `vd`). At each further level DETECTOR-NULL kills the minor children and the
   307	major ones continue the tower; the tower stops at `D_1`, because at `r = 1` the
   308	minor criterion reads `#roots <= n/(n-M_1) = n/(n+m) < 1` — no nonempty disc is
   309	minor — and there is no `M_0`.
   310	
   311	> **THEOREM N-CEILING.** For a degree-minimal Jacobian counterexample in Moh's
   312	> gauge with tower data `(n, m, M_*, d_*, V_*)`,
   313	> ```text
   314	>     N  <=  U(skeleton)  :=  u * d * (-lambda_g(delta_1))^+
   315	>                          =  u * d * e * (1 - delta_1) / (d + e) ,
   316	>            u = V_s K / d_s ,  deg P = m = Kd ,  deg Q = n = Ke = D .
   317	> ```
   318	> In particular `lambda_g(delta_1) >= 0` (equivalently `delta_1 >= 1`) is
   319	> **impossible**: it would force `N = 0`.
   320	
   321	*Proof.* By FRONTIER-N, `N = sum_i(-lambda_f^{(i)}(delta^0_i))^+`, and
   322	`lambda_f` is nondecreasing, so for `rho_i` in a disc `B` with
   323	`delta(B) <= delta^0_i` the term is `<= (-lambda_f(delta(B)))^+`. Cover the
   324	`g`-roots by the maximal minor discs together with the bottom-major discs. The
   325	minor part contributes `0` (DETECTOR-NULL). The bottom-major discs are disjoint
   326	subsets of `D_{s-1}` (the unique major child of the root ball), so their `g`-root
   327	counts total `<= a_{s-1} = ue`; on each,
   328	`-lambda_f(delta_1) = (d/e)(-lambda_g(delta_1))` (§4.1). Hence
   329	`N <= ue(d/e)(-lambda_g(delta_1)) = ud(-lambda_g(delta_1))`; the closed form is
   330	RADIUS-ORDER at `r = 1` with `M_1 = -m`, `n+m = K(d+e)`, `n = Ke`. If
   331	`lambda_g(delta_1) >= 0` the same covering gives `N = 0`; but `N = 1` is the
   332	invertible case (Keller ⟹ étale; degree 1 ⟹ birational ⟹ injective ⟹ surjective
   333	by Ax–Grothendieck ⟹ automorphism), so a counterexample has `N >= 2`. ∎
   334	
   335	> **COROLLARY HARMONIC-BOUND (unconditional in the stated scope).** Moh Lemma 6.1
   336	> gives `delta_{s-1} >= 0`, and radii increase downward, so `delta_1 >= 0` and
   337	> `1 - delta_1 <= 1`; `v >= 1` gives `u <= K - 1`. Hence
   338	> ```text
   339	>     N  <  K d e/(d+e)  =  m n/(m + n) ,     i.e.     1/N  >  1/deg P + 1/deg Q ,
   340	> ```
   341	> and since `d < e`, `N < D * d/(d+e) < D/2`.
   342	
   343	Sanity: for `(x, y + x^k)` the corollary would read `N < k/(k+1) < 1`, false —
   344	correctly so, since there `nu = 1`, `delta_s > -1`, and neither NU-TWO nor
   345	Lemma 6.1 applies. Measured: `delta_{s-1} >= 0` and `delta_1 >= 0` on **all
   346	1 260 149** V-skeletons with `n <= 130` and on **all 3 874 261** branch-robust
   347	groups with `D <= 400`, 0 exceptions; `U < mn/(m+n)` on all 3 874 261, 0
   348	exceptions.
   349	
   350	> **COROLLARY RAMIFICATION-FLOOR.** At a **proper** place `gamma`,
   351	> `m_gamma = nu_gamma(-lambda_f(delta^0)) <= nu_gamma(-lambda_f(delta_1))`, so
   352	> `nu_gamma >= m_gamma/(-lambda_f(delta_1)) = m_gamma u e/U`; for (64,48) with
   353	> Moh's `V`, `nu_gamma >= 16 m_gamma/3 >= 6` at every proper place. This answers
   354	> DC's `OPEN[NU-BOUND-AT-A-PLACE]` in the **direction opposite** to the one it
   355	> wants: the tree gives a FLOOR on the ramification, never a ceiling, so
   356	> `T <= sum h(m_gamma)` is not reachable this way (§8 F).
