   472	
   473	### 6.3 Why the unconditional filter can never fire, and what the H2 filter kills
   474	
   475	Letting the lower `V_j -> infinity` in the closed form, `P_j/Q_j -> (n-M_j)/(n-M_{j-1})`,
   476	the product telescopes and
   477	`sup U = (u-v)(de/(d+e)) * V_s(n-M_{s-1})/(V_s(n-M_{s-1}) - d_s) > (u-v)de/(d+e)`.
   478	Minimising over the data (`2V_s - d_s = 1`, so `u-v = K/d_s`; `d_s <= K/2`;
   479	`(d,e) = (2,3)`) gives the asymptotic floor `2de/(d+e) = 12/5 = 2.4`; the measured
   480	global minimum over 3 874 261 groups is `792/329 = 2.4073`. **`U > 2` always, so
   481	`N <= U` never contradicts `N >= 2`.**
   482	
   483	The `U < 4` kills are therefore confined to `(u-v)de/(d+e) < 4`, i.e.
   484	`u - v < 4(d+e)/(de) <= 10/3`: **the H2 filter kills exactly (a subset of) the
   485	skeletons whose top form is nearly balanced.** Measured over `D <= 200`:
   486	`U_rob > (u-v)de/(d+e)` on all 120 641 groups (min ratio `342/341`), and every
   487	killed group has `u - v in {2,3}` — e.g. `n = 90, m = 60, K = 30, d_s = 15,
   488	V_s = 8, (u,v) = (16,14)`, `U = 192/79 = 2.430`.
