   520	## 7. Part (5): controls on the filter
   521	
   522	**(a) `N = 1` skeletons — accepted by the pairing, rejected by non-invertibility.**
   523	`(y, x + y^k)` has `N = 1` and the pairing computes it exactly (CONTROL 2). On the
   524	skeleton side `m = 1`, so `d_2 = gcd(n,1) = 1`: the chain dies at once, `s = 1 < 3`
   525	(Prop 5.5), `d_s = 1 < 4` (Cor 6.1), `K = 1 < 16` (GGV Cor 6.6) — three
   526	independent rejections, and the automorphism never enters the census.
   527	Geometrically the same fact is `nu = 1`, i.e. `delta_s > -1`, which Prop 5.4 turns
   528	into a degree reduction.
   529	
   530	**(b) Non-Keller families — rejected at the Jacobian steps.** For each of the
   531	seven two-tower rows the deliverable computes the bracket of the **top forms**,
   532	`[l(f),l(g)]`, whose vanishing is the first consequence of the Jacobian condition
   533	((LF)). Five of the seven have `[l(f),l(g)] != 0` and are rejected **there**; the
   534	two with `l(f) = H^2`, `l(g) = H^3` pass (LF) with `(d,e) = (2,3)` and are rejected
   535	at `K = gcd(m,n) in {2,4} < 16` (GGV Cor 6.6, itself a Jacobian theorem). All
   536	seven have non-constant Jacobian (checked), so it is visible *which* step rejects
   537	each.
   538	
   539	**(c) Positive control on the recursion, and census-wide consistency.** Moh's
   540	published `delta` columns reproduced exactly from an independent implementation of
   541	Def 5.1(3): the four legible pairs `(1/4,9/16)`, `(2/7,16/21)`, `(1/4,7/12)`,
   542	`(1/3,4/9)` all MATCH, and the two illegible `n = 75` rows are predicted
   543	`(1/5,1/2)`, `(1/5,2/3)`, agreeing with DC's independent prediction; all Def 5.1(2)
   544	windows hold and `delta_s = -1`, `u+v = K`, `u > v`, `a_{s-1} = ue`,
   545	`b_i/a_i = m/n` on every row. RADIUS-ORDER, the product form of `lambda_g` and the
   546	closed `N-CEILING` agree with the incremental computation on all 242 099
   547	V-skeletons at `n <= 100` (0 failures); `delta_1 >= delta_{s-1} >= 0` and radii
   548	strictly increasing downward on all 1 260 149 V-skeletons at `n <= 130`
   549	(0 exceptions, consistent with Lemma 6.1) and on all 3 874 261 branch-robust
   550	groups with `D <= 400`; the top-of-window `V` realises the branch-robust maximum
   551	on all 3975 groups at `D <= 100` (0 mismatches against brute force).
