A concrete crack has emerged: on a branch \(g(x,\tau)=c_2\), the Jacobian equation gives the exact ODE
\[
\frac{d}{dx}f(x,\tau(x))=\frac1{g_y(x,\tau(x))}.
\]
So the missing \(D_1\) contact is not merely a free two-colour ultrametric tree; it must also match the self-different of the \(g\)-fibre. I’m checking whether the banked record already consumed this identity and whether its global form—an infinity-supported, nowhere-affine-ramified pencil—offers a genuine right-direction invariant.
