xmodel/max12-812-order4-lemniscatic-target-corollary-review-grok-20260826.md:251:On any short Weierstrass model with `Delta\neq 0`, `dX/Z` is a basis of `H^0(E,Omega^1)`. Locally at the origin of (7), `Z_E^2=-16 X_E+\cdots` gives `d X_E/Z_E=-d Z_E/8+\cdots`, regular and nonvanishing. At the point at infinity, the standard parameter `u=X_E/Z_E` has `X_E=u^{-2}+\cdots`, `Z_E=-u^{-3}+\cdots`, hence `d X_E/Z_E=2\,du`, regular and nonvanishing in characteristic zero. The form is therefore a nonzero regular differential on the complete curve (7). Transport along the isomorphism of Attack 3 makes `-d xi/W` a nonzero regular differential on `Y~`. It is not the zero section of `Omega^1`, and it has no poles.
