xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:34:**F3. Adamus–Hajto, *On the Jung–van der Kulk decomposition into Pascal finite factors*, arXiv:2607.09340v1, 2026-07-10.** SHA-256 `3e7c10f7c1c322ffe1a61d8f328b6ae14b63ff5bba269f716fcaf34d0cdb250a`. Every plane automorphism fixing the origin factors as a diagonal Jacobian times Pascal-finite automorphisms; \(\det J_F=1\) iff \(F\) is a composition of Pascal-finite maps, in any characteristic. An analogue of the Exponential Generators Conjecture in dim 2. **IRRELEVANT** to noninvertible Keller maps; it classifies automorphisms.
xmodel/web-sweep-20260902-grok46.md:72:**F14. Orevkov, *On germs of mappings \(\mathbb{C}^2\to\mathbb{C}^2\)*, arXiv:2512.07986v1, 2025-12-08.** SHA-256 `a25645002759138455b64db053c00771f4cf203d6ec386d2c33969ecffe94065` (31 pp.). **Campaign miss** (grep of `2512.07986` empty). Addendum to Kulikov 2503.07099 (F15). Classifies analytic germs \(F:(\mathbb{C}^2,0)\to(\mathbb{C}^2,0)\) that are finite covers of degree \(N\), branched over \(C=\{u^{d_1}=v^{d_2}\}\) with \(\gcd(d_1,d_2)=1\) and \(\min(d_1,d_2)>1\), under (A1)–(A2): \(F\) analytic, \(F(0)=0\), and \(F\) bijective on each component of \(F^{-1}(C)\). Ramification order \(n\) along the singular locus \(\widetilde C\) means \(\mathrm{div}(JF)=(n-1)\widetilde C\). Completeness: every such germ is, after swapping \(d_1\leftrightarrow d_2\), one of two Belyi/Davenport–Zannier families (a)/(b), built from a Belyi function with ramification type \((\alpha;(n,1^{N-1});\beta)\). Explicit formulae for \(n=2\) (quadratic ramification) and half of \(n=3\). Uses Orevkov 2001 “JC at infinity” toric-cover machinery (his [8], with a recorded misprint in §1.2). Jacobian identity is \(J(F)=\mu(y^{k_2}-x^{k_1})^{n-1}\), **not a constant**. **STRUCTURE** for the local ramified model of a one-cusp (torus-knot) branch, for HOM-COVER’s local covering data, and for Chisini-type uniqueness of surfaces from ramification images. **IRRELEVANT as a threat** to NO-PUSHFORWARD / CENTRAL-RANK (those are global homology of \(S_n\)-covers of affine complements). Does **not** produce an \(S_4\) cover of a realized \((9,6,*)\) curve.
