+# Blind ideation submission — round 20260902T1608Z — Sol 5.6 ultra
+
+Charged packet SHA-256: `ab66bd6b87dc035740325c309349ec8d52a5963b6b1a0a6e0e53a34f74715af3` (verified before reading). Frozen campaign basis: `7f7c0306768d`. Scope: blind full-spectrum response to `OPEN[UPPER-TO-FLOOR]`; banked reports only; no `jc2-lean`; no canonical-ledger edits.
+
+## 1. Direct verdict
+
+The coordinator is right about the record and wrong if the reading is promoted one quantifier further.
+
+The right statement is: **every boundary instrument currently built, including Moh's published skeleton, is one-directional.** `N-CEILING` gives `N <= U`; extra structure below `D_1` adds contact and lowers `N`; the filter `N <= 16` therefore cannot reject a skeleton (`xmodel/integration16-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:38-54`; `xmodel/n-on-the-tree-review-grok46-20260902.md:143-153`). The 418 rows are necessary H2 realization targets, not maps, and “pinned to 4” consumes the H2 floor `N >= 4` (`xmodel/n-on-the-tree-review-grok46-20260902.md:191-218,334-345`). No ceiling has been proved.
+
+The overstatement is: **the lane has not proved that the boundary route itself can never give a floor.** The interval
+
+```text
+0 <= N|D_1 <= a_1(-lambda_f(delta_1))
+```
+
+is the range allowed by Moh's skeleton and abstract ultrametric completion. Its lower endpoint is not attained by an actual Keller pair. The review says explicitly that the full Jacobian may constrain the subtree and that Moh does not (`xmodel/n-on-the-tree-review-grok46-20260902.md:137-151`). Integration #16 itself reserves exactly this exception (`xmodel/integration16-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:109-115`). Thus “as built” is correct; “no boundary argument” is not licensed. Candidate (f) must be stated as a no-go for arguments factoring through Moh (1)–(13) plus the major skeleton, not for arguments using new Jacobian coefficients below `D_1`.
+
+There is also a plain factual error in candidate (c). APPROACHES row 20 was run as a standalone formalism lane on 2026-08-23. The canonical inverse-Jacobian connection has identically zero p-curvature, while Tsuchimoto's non-tautological object starts with a Weyl-algebra endomorphism and is not defined on an arbitrary commutative Keller map (`xmodel/sol-pcurvature.md:3-30,423-426,501-528`). That branch is `KNOWN-HOLLOW/retire`, not “never run.” Finite-field realization remains a different, one-way falsification tool.
+
+My allocation answer is consequently direct. Give `D_1` one bounded, exact pilot. If it does not expose a positive Jacobian deficiency at the first post-`delta_1` levels, stop treating a universal `D <= C(N)` as the primary proof target. Move the proof flagship to the Moh endgame—uniform elimination of finite-depth, unbounded-size skeletons—and run the exact same `D_1` machinery backwards on the counterexample side. Keep a small global-invariant probe, but do not fund five speculative ceiling languages at once. The depth count is finite; the coefficients and sizes are not. That is an elimination/realization problem, not evidence that another scalar ledger is waiting to be found.
+
+## 2. A new exact cross-connection: the `D_1` self-different
+
+The missing joint `f`/`g` subtree can be reduced to a one-colour subtree before any large computation. Work in Moh's monic gauge, put `t=x^{-1}`, take generic `c_2`, and let `tau_i` be the Puiseux roots of `g-c_2`. Set
+
+```text
+h_i(x) = f(x,tau_i(x)).
+```
+
+Implicit differentiation and `[f,g]=1` give the exact branch identity
+
+```text
+d h_i/dx = f_x - f_y g_x/g_y = 1/g_y(x,tau_i).                 (SD1)
+```
+
+If `h_i` has pole order `p_i=-ord_t h_i>0`, then differentiation changes the `t`-order from `-p_i` to `1-p_i`, hence
+
+```text
+p_i = 1 + ord_t g_y(x,tau_i).
+```
+
+If `h_i` is finite, its first nonconstant algebraic term has positive rational `t`-order, so `1+ord_t g_y<0`; equality zero would integrate to a logarithm and cannot occur in the Puiseux field. Because `g` is monic,
+
+```text
+g_y(x,tau_i) = product_{j != i}(tau_i-tau_j).
+```
+
+Combining this with CONTACT-DEFICIENCY yields the exact, review-needed formula
+
+```text
+N = sum_i max(0, 1 + ord_t g_y(x,tau_i))
+  = sum_i max(0, 1 + sum_{j != i} ord_t(tau_i-tau_j)).          (SD2)
+```
+
+This is not a lower bound and I do not promote one. It is a new representation of the missing datum: `N` is computable from the self-contact tree of `g-c_2`; the `b_1=dV_2` roots of `f` need not be enumerated. FRONTIER-N put `N` on the joint tree of `f*g` (`xmodel/n-on-the-tree-opus5-20260902.md:174-206`). `(SD2)` uses the Jacobian equation to project it to the one-coordinate different. The remaining freedom is now exactly the self-tree of the `a_1=eV_2` roots below `D_1`, not an arbitrary two-colour pairing.
+
+This also connects two lanes that the present ranking keeps separate. For a fixed candidate `g`, finding `f` is the linear Hamiltonian equation `[f,g]=1`; the banked kappa class vanishes exactly when a polynomial mate exists (`xmodel/hamiltonian-kappa-gate-20260824.md:49-80`). The kappa module has no universal receiver and remains a bad global ceiling strategy (`xmodel/hamiltonian-kappa-gate-20260824.md:180-198`), but on one typed `D_1` skeleton it is an exact obstruction/certificate engine. Candidate (d) should therefore be lowered as a global flow proposal and reused as the local solver inside candidate (a).
+
+The first cheap gate is the no-log condition in `(SD1)`: every branchwise Laurent expansion of `dx/g_y` must have zero residue before it can be the differential of an algebraic `h_i`. Passing that gate is not a Keller witness; failing it is an exact rejection of the proposed self-tree. This is the strongest proof attack in this submission.
+
+## 3. Disposition vectors
+
+Codes are `U` unchanged, `R` raise, `L` lower, and `RT` retype. This is a full 46-entry vector; reasons follow only for changes, as charged.
+
+```text
+ 1 RT   2 RT   3 U    4 U    5 RT   6 U    7 RT   8 U    9 U   10 U
+11 U   12 U   13 U   14 U   15 U   16 U   17 U   18 U   19 U   20 RT
+21 U   22 U   23 U   24 U   25 RT  26 R   27 RT  28 L   29 U   30 U
+31 U   32 U   33 U   34 U   35 U   36 R   37 U   38 U   39 U   40 U
+41 U   42 U   43 U   44 U   45 U   46 U
+```
+
+| Row | Change | Reason |
+|---:|---|---|
+| 1, GGV corner farm | `RT` | Finite-depth/unbounded-size Moh endgame and typed realization program, not a cofinal degree farm. “Always a next pair” is false as a count; pair size and the bottom subtree remain free (`xmodel/integration15-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:28-36`). |
+| 2, sheet/Eggers–Wall/boundary trees | `RT` | Classifier, `N`-upper-bound, and realization instrument. It pins windows but is not presently a `D`-ceiling route (`xmodel/integration16-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:38-63,100-105`). |
+| 5, Jung–van der Kulk/Aut | `RT` | Now substantive infrastructure: orbit-minimality gives a degree-preserving affine source change into the subrectangular gauge. It still supplies no degree-lowering elementary automorphism (`xmodel/integration15-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:11-19`). |
+| 7, `A_F`/nonproperness | `RT` | The source curve `E` and its additive/log-Chern package have now been tried; those invariants scale and do not cross. Retain nonadditive representation data and realization of `A_F`, not another Euler/BMY count (`xmodel/integration10-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:12-40`). |
+| 20, p-curvature | `RT` | Tried and retired as an independent commutative Keller obstruction, contrary to the packet. The automatic connection has zero p-curvature; the useful Tsuchimoto direction has the wrong source (`xmodel/sol-pcurvature.md:14-30,522-528`). |
+| 25, fibre monodromy/passports | `RT` | Scalar passports, total `H_1`, and vanishing-cycle rank are now exact Riemann–Hurwitz/Euler identities. Only coupled two-coordinate or isotypic representation data remain live (`xmodel/keller-pencil-genus-opus5-20260902.md:105-140,375-380`). |
+| 26, primitive monodromy/Galois | `R` narrowly | Test character-valued Chevalley–Weil multiplicities on the N=4 H2 cover. Do not repeat total-H1 or total-genus counts. A single `S_4` virtual-character computation is the launch gate. |
+| 27, links/splice/plumbing | `RT` | Use as an attainment/realisability filter on pinned skeletons, not as a scalar ceiling. Topology can reject a proposed completion even though the major skeleton alone only upper-bounds `N`. |
+| 28, log surfaces/BMY | `L` | BMY on `E` and on its Galois closure is proved vacuous by scaling; Noether, genus, and total vanishing-cycle ledgers reproduce identities (`xmodel/integration10-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:16-25`; `xmodel/integration13-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:22-32,47-63`). |
+| 36, guided counterexample search | `R` narrowly | For the first time it has a finite structural target: branch-robust H2 skeleton groups pinned to `N=4`. Replace generic SAT/fewnomial search by skeleton-conditioned Laurent realization, starting at D=105. |
+
+All other rows stay `U`. In particular rows 29 and 33 are not globally reopened: Hamiltonian exactness has no universal receiver and untwisted symplectic residues are automatic. Their exact identities may be used inside the fixed `D_1` client without changing their portfolio status.
+
+### Candidates (a)–(f)
+
+| Candidate | Disposition and rank | Reason |
+|---|---|---|
+| (a) Jacobian below `D_1` | `R`, rank 1 | Only untested boundary location; run one exact target. The bounded datum is `N|D_1` in its reviewed interval, and full Jacobian constraints are explicitly not consumed by Moh. |
+| (f) boundary one-directionality theorem | `R`, rank 2, coupled to (a) | Prove a schema-limited no-go: Moh (1)–(13), major-tree data, and ultrametric axioms admit same-skeleton completions with different deficiencies. Promote a stronger `UPPER-ONLY` statement only if the Jacobian-jet pilot also admits the lower endpoint. |
+| (b) global invariant | `RT`, rank 3 | Lower additive `E` invariants and total pencil `H_1`; raise only isotypic Galois `H_1` and the pointed étale-gonality mechanism in Card 2. |
+| (e) analytic growth | `U` low, rank 4 | It has the right desired sign but no named inequality or receiver. Require an exact toy inequality that survives automorphisms in `D_min` gauge and a non-Keller polynomial-submersion control before launch. |
+| (d) Hamiltonian flows | `L`, rank 5 | Completeness/LND is essentially the conjecture and the kappa class is an exact reformulation. Reuse the linear mate obstruction locally under (a); do not launch a global dynamics lane. |
+| (c) characteristic p | `RT/L`, rank 6 | Stop p-curvature as proof engine; it already ran. Keep finite-field/Witt computations only as falsifiers or lifting diagnostics for one typed integral realization system. Positive modular points never constitute a characteristic-zero map. |
+
+### Deferred fronts
+
+1. **Moh endgame: raise to co-flagship.** Bound the first campaign slice as the number of realizable groups at `D=105`, an integer in `[0,264]`; do not call an all-D enumeration finite merely because depth is log-bounded.
+2. **Pinned-N=4 realization: raise.** The first slice is the Boolean realization of the exact D=105 group in Section 7. This is the best disproof front.
+3. **General reducible branch: raise modestly and keep distinct from the already-closed reducible rank-four proper-block branch.** H2 cannot by itself resolve unconditional JC2; integration #16 explicitly leaves the reducible branch untouched (`xmodel/integration16-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:7-10,121-123`).
+4. **A2: unchanged deferred.** It is an untyped map-germ with two repaired P0s, not the B3 horn. No event in this packet repairs the typing arrow.
+5. **B3 degree-5/6 census: lower/stop as a window route.** Exact rows without a general-N assembly theorem gave no legal pruning and were demoted (`xmodel/integration14-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:64-71`). Preserve the data; launch no wider census.

