The new Jacobian identity is stronger than expected. For each bottom-major disc, the self-contact lower bound from \(g_y=\prod_{j\ne i}(\tau_i-\tau_j)\) exactly meets FRONTIER-N’s upper bound. The supposedly free contribution is therefore a fixed rational weight, branch by branch. I’m now stress-testing the resulting rational knapsack on all 59 pinned groups; this is the first genuinely two-sided filter in the record, so I’m treating every branch-heterogeneity and attainment qualification as load-bearing.
