+The first cheap gate is the no-log condition in `(SD1)`: every branchwise Laurent expansion of `dx/g_y` must have zero residue before it can be the differential of an algebraic `h_i`. Passing that gate is not a Keller witness; failing it is an exact rejection of the proposed self-tree. This is the strongest proof attack in this submission.
