+## 7. Software acceleration
+
+Add a fail-closed `--exact-n-weight 4 --jsonl` mode to `box/moh_skeleton_N.py`; do not create a second enumerator. The existing program already uses exact `Fraction` arithmetic and distinguishes the published-tower bound from the branch-robust maximum (`box/moh_skeleton_N.py:27-28,401-407`). The new mode should make the following join explicit:
+
+```text
+Moh group
+  -> all one-bottom-branch full-V rows
+  -> exact (V_2, delta_1, lambda_f, q=eV_2, w=-q lambda_f)
+  -> permissive rational DP under sum V_2 <= u
+  -> orbit-packet DP under Moh (8)--(11)
+  -> no-log residue gate
+  -> sparse polynomial-mate system
+```
+
+Each JSONL record should contain `D,m,K,d,e,M,d_chain,V_s,u,v,U_rob`, the complete typed branch list, the attainable rational `N` set, and status in the chain
+
+```text
+SKELETON -> WEIGHT_HIT -> ORBIT_HIT -> RESIDUE_HIT -> MATE_HIT.
+```
+
+The program must fail closed if two full-`V` rows map to the same displayed branch key with different radii, if a rational weight has not been normalized, or if the rows have not been certified exhaustive for the fixed group. It must never label `WEIGHT_HIT` as `REALIZABLE`. The negative control is the D=105, `M_2=-35` group (no weight-4 hit); the positive arithmetic control is the D=105, `M_2=56` four-unit multiset; the map-level control is `(f,g)=(y,x+y^k)`, whose `k` branch contributions sum to one. Regression counts before orbit constraints are exactly
+
+```text
+old groups:       (14,40,0,0,5) at D=(105,108,112,117,120)
+weight survivors: ( 3,16,0,0,2).
+```
+
+This is the decisive software acceleration because it changes the unit of work from a maximum attached to a skeleton to a finite exact packet that the coefficient solver can consume. Its bounded full run is the 418 reviewed pin-4 groups for `101 <= D <= 200`; only after that regression passes should it be extended to the larger census. Do not raise the search cap merely to collect more maxima.
