+## 6. Idea cards (three only)
+
+### Card 1 — D1-SELF-DIFFERENT and exact-weight filter (`NEW`)
+
+**Mechanism.** Use the Jacobian ODE `(SD1)` to express `N` through the shifted `g`-root different, prove the matching inequalities `(SD3)`–`(SD5)`, and replace `N <= U_rob` by the exact branch-weight equation `(SD6)`. This is the requested lower-to-floor mechanism: it injects the Jacobian below `D_1`, where Moh stops, rather than adding another boundary ledger.
+
+**Dependencies.** Monic `deg=deg_y` gauge; characteristic zero; generic squarefree `g-c_2`; FRONTIER-N; RADIUS-ORDER with `M_1=-m`; DETECTOR-NULL; the fact that shifted roots preserve the clipped tree down to `delta_1`; disjoint bottom-major discs; exhaustive one-branch lower-`V` rows. No H2 is used in the identity; H2 supplies `N>=4` in the first filter.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.** A different-model hand proof on one bottom disc plus three controls: `(y,x+y^k)` gives `k` contributions `1/k` and total `N=1`; the D=105 `M_2=-35` group has no permissive weight-4 packet; the D=105 `M_2=56` group has the explicit four-weight hit. Then implement the 59-row regression and audit all vanished-leader/radius branches.
+
+**Interpretation of outcomes.** If the proof and controls pass, the coordinator's categorical one-directionality reading is false and the campaign owns a two-sided finite filter. If `(SD3)` fails, identify the first shifted-root contact that can become smaller than its clipped unshifted contact; that is the exact flaw and Card 1 stops. If the formula is correct but all 418 rows retain a packet, it still removes joint-subtree enumeration and hands exact inputs to the Moh endgame. If the full filter empties the 418, that closes those necessary N=4 skeleton targets, not N=4 itself unless coverage of all admissible degrees is separately proved.
+
+**Stop condition.** Stop promotion on any failure of monicity, root association, branch-type exhaustiveness, or orbit accounting. Stop scaling the DP once exact orbit constraints leave a stable large family with no uniform obstruction; pass those finite packets to coefficient elimination.
+
+**Expected information gain.** Very high. A 26-second permissive prototype already changed 59 candidates to 21 and supplies a theorem-level explanation rather than a larger census.
+
+### Card 2 — D=105 four-unit packet realization (`NEW APPLICATION`)
+
+**Mechanism.** Work backwards from the simplest permissive survivor: `(M_2,V_s)=(56,4)` with four `V_2=3` bottom branches, each exact weight one. Construct a Galois-stable shifted-root tree for `g-c_2`; reconstruct branch values of `f` by integrating `dx/g_y`; then solve the global linear mate equation in the finite coefficient box `deg f<=42`, `deg g<=105`. The same computation is adversarial: failure yields a missing Moh-endgame condition; success yields the sharpest counterexample seed.
+
+**Dependencies.** Card 1; complete orbit packets; Moh (8)–(11); subrectangular leading form `H=x^{12}y^9` after affine normalization; exact coefficient field and monic generator order; resultant degree in the declared quotient; characteristic-zero coefficients. H2 is used only to select `N=4`, not to infer a map.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.** Before emitting full coefficients, test whether four copies of the `V_2=3` branch type form legal Puiseux conjugacy orbits and attach inside the 60-root major class. Next run the branchwise residue/no-log gate on `dx/g_y`. Both are rational arithmetic. Only then build the sparse Jacobian linear system.
+
+**Interpretation of outcomes.** Orbit or residue failure kills this packet exactly and promotes the failed condition into Moh's search. A finite linear inconsistency kills the typed coefficient family. An all-order formal solution is a formal survivor only. A polynomial pair with `J=1` must still pass resultant `N=4`, nonproperness, H2 profile, and noninvertibility; failure at any arrow is diagnostic, not a counterexample. A full pass is a genuine JC2 counterexample candidate and triggers independent exact replay immediately.
+
+**Stop condition.** Stop after the first exact obstruction and generalize it before trying another support. Stop the disproof claim at `FORMAL` if algebraization or global degree is absent. Do not widen to D=108/120 until every D=105 permissive packet is classified.
+
+**Expected information gain.** High and symmetric: either a new uniform elimination rule or the first coefficient-level seed tied to geometric degree rather than merely to a top form.
+
+### Card 3 — isotypic Galois-closure homology (`NEW RECEIVER, LOW-COST GATE`)
+
+**Mechanism.** Candidate (b) should not ask for total `H_1`; that is already Riemann–Hurwitz. On the generic target line, pass to the Galois closure of the degree-N cover and compute `H_1` as a rational `G`-module. Local inertia contributes induced characters, so nonnegative integral multiplicities of each irreducible representation are stricter data than the scalar Euler characteristic. At N=4 with H2 meridian type `1^2 2`, a transitive group generated by the finite transpositions is `S_4`; the first gate is therefore finite and explicit.
+
+**Dependencies.** A typed branch-cycle tuple including infinity, not just cycle counts; connected generic line cover; tame characteristic zero; exact distinction between source `E`, line cover, and Galois closure. E-BMY scaling and total pencil homology are negative controls, not inputs to a claimed inequality.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.** For each existing N=4 passport row, compute the Chevalley–Weil/Lefschetz virtual character from finite transposition inertia and the infinity permutation; decompose it into the five rational irreducibles of `S_4`. Check nonnegative integral multiplicities. Run a genuine four-sheet cover as a positive control and the scalar dimension against MF-EXACT.
+
+**Interpretation of outcomes.** A negative/fractional multiplicity kills the branch-cycle row globally without a boundary-size ceiling. If every virtual character is effective and depends only on scalar RH data, candidate (b) collapses to the known identity and stops. If only some isotypic component constrains the infinity permutation, couple that component—not total `H_1`—to the D1 packet.
+
+**Stop condition.** One complete N=4 pass with every row effective and no information beyond scalar RH. Do not build a surface Galois closure or invoke BMY after that negative result.
+
+**Expected information gain.** Medium. The gate is cheap and genuinely nonadditive, but Card 1 is much closer to the live obstruction.
